  <!-- FAQ Section -->
  <Fragment slot="faq">
    <section class="py-16 lg:py-24 bg-white">
      <Container>
        <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto" data-reveal>
          <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-[family-name:var(--font-heading)] text-dark-text mb-10 text-center">
            Bathtub Replacement FAQs
          </h2>
          <div class="space-y-4">
            <details class="group bg-light rounded-xl border border-border">
              <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer p-6 font-semibold text-dark-text font-[family-name:var(--font-heading)] text-lg">
                How much does bathtub replacement cost?
                <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-5 h-5 text-muted transition-transform group-open:rotate-180" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
                  <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
                </svg>
              </summary>
              <div class="px-6 pb-6 text-muted leading-relaxed">
                A standard alcove tub replacement in Seattle typically costs $3,000-$6,000, including the tub, plumbing, and basic surround finishing. Freestanding tub installations range from $5,000-$12,000+ depending on the tub material, faucet selection, and floor work required. Japanese soaking tubs and models with jet systems cost more due to the specialized plumbing and electrical work involved.
              </div>
            </details>
            <details class="group bg-light rounded-xl border border-border">
              <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer p-6 font-semibold text-dark-text font-[family-name:var(--font-heading)] text-lg">
                How long does a bathtub replacement take?
                <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-5 h-5 text-muted transition-transform group-open:rotate-180" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
                  <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
                </svg>
              </summary>
              <div class="px-6 pb-6 text-muted leading-relaxed">
                A straightforward alcove tub swap can be completed in 2-3 days. Installations requiring subfloor repair, plumbing rerouting, or tile surround work take 4-7 days. Freestanding tub installations with floor modification typically take 3-5 days. We provide a detailed timeline specific to your project during the consultation.
              </div>
            </details>
            <details class="group bg-light rounded-xl border border-border">
              <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer p-6 font-semibold text-dark-text font-[family-name:var(--font-heading)] text-lg">
                Can my floor support a freestanding tub?
                <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-5 h-5 text-muted transition-transform group-open:rotate-180" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
                  <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
                </svg>
              </summary>
              <div class="px-6 pb-6 text-muted leading-relaxed">
                It depends on the tub material and your floor structure. An acrylic freestanding tub filled with water weighs 300-400 lbs and is typically fine for standard floor joists. A cast-iron tub filled with water can weigh 800-1,200 lbs and may require joist reinforcement. We evaluate your floor structure during the consultation and include any necessary reinforcement in our proposal.
              </div>
            </details>
            <details class="group bg-light rounded-xl border border-border">
              <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer p-6 font-semibold text-dark-text font-[family-name:var(--font-heading)] text-lg">
                Should I replace or refinish my bathtub?
                <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-5 h-5 text-muted transition-transform group-open:rotate-180" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
                  <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
                </svg>
              </summary>
              <div class="px-6 pb-6 text-muted leading-relaxed">
                Refinishing (reglazing) can extend a tub's life by 5-10 years at a lower cost. However, replacement is the better long-term investment if your tub has cracks, chips, or structural damage, or if you want to change the tub type, size, or style. We can assess your tub's condition during a free consultation and recommend the best option for your situation and budget.
              </div>
            </details>
          </div>
        </div>
      </Container>
    </section>
  </Fragment>

